/*!
    \class vsmm::IModStore
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Interface of the mod store, declares the signals between the backend libraries.

    IModStore is the abstract base of \l vsmm::ModStore. The other backend
    libraries depend on this interface instead of \l vsmm::ModStore, so
    their tests can use a mock store.

    The signals tell the list models, the update model, the image provider
    and \l vsmm::ModLoader about changes to the installed mods and about the
    state of mod updates. The public slots receive progress and results from
    the loader. \l vsmm::ModLoader connects to modsReloading(),
    modUpdateRequested() and onModsReloaded() in its \c setStore() function
    and calls the other slots directly.
*/

/*!
    \enum vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType

    Tells add() where a mod zip comes from.

    \value Init
        The zip is in a mods folder and was found by a scan of the mods
        folders, at startup or on a reload.
    \value GUI
        The zip was passed to the QML invokable \c load() of
        \l vsmm::ModLoader. \l vsmm::ModStore copies it into the mods
        folder, or treats it as an update when a mod with the same id is
        already installed.
    \value Update
        The zip is a downloaded update of an installed mod.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::IModStore::IModStore(QObject *parent)

    Constructs the store with the given \a parent.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::IModStore::~IModStore()

    Destroys the store.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::add(vsmm::ModLocalInfo localModInfo, vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType loadType)

    Adds the mod described by \a localModInfo to the store. \a loadType tells
    where the mod zip comes from.

    \sa ModLoadType
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::updateOnline(QStringView id, QJsonObject onlineInfo)

    Sets the online info of the mod \a id. \a onlineInfo is the \c mod object
    of the mod API response.
*/

/*!
    \fn const vsmm::ModEntry *vsmm::IModStore::find(const QString &id) const

    Returns the mod with the id \a id, or \c nullptr when no such mod is
    installed.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modAdded(QStringView modId)

    This signal is emitted after the mod \a modId is added to the store.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdated(QStringView modId)

    This signal is emitted after the data of the installed mod \a modId
    changes, for example when its online info arrives or a newer version
    replaces it.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modsReloading()

    This signal is emitted when a reload starts, before the store drops its
    mods. The entries are still readable while the signal is handled.
    \l vsmm::ModLoader starts a new scan of the mods folders on this signal.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modRemoved(QStringView modId)

    This signal is emitted when the mod \a modId is removed, after its file
    is deleted and before the store drops the entry.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateRequested(QStringList modIds)

    This signal is emitted when \l vsmm::ModStore starts an update of the
    mods \a modIds, from \c update(), \c updateAll() or \c updateSelected(). \l vsmm::ModLoader downloads the updates on this signal.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateProgress(QStringView modId, qint64 received, qint64 total)

    This signal is emitted while the update of the mod \a modId downloads.
    \a received is the number of bytes received so far and \a total the
    size of the download.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateInstalling(QStringView modId)

    This signal is emitted when the store starts to replace the installed
    mod \a modId with a new zip.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateFinished(QStringView modId)

    This signal is emitted after the update of the mod \a modId is
    installed.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateFailed(QStringView modId, QString reason)

    This signal is emitted when the update of the mod \a modId fails.
    \a reason is a message that says why.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::modsLoaded()

    This signal is emitted when the loader has no loads or downloads left in
    progress.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::onModsReloaded()

    Called when the loader has no loads or downloads left in progress.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::onModUpdateProgress(const QString &modId, qint64 received, qint64 total)

    Called while the update of the mod \a modId downloads. \a received is the
    number of bytes received so far and \a total the size of the download.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::IModStore::onModUpdateFailed(QString modId, QString reason)

    Called when the update of the mod \a modId fails before it reaches the
    store. \a reason is a message that says why.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModStore
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Holds the installed mods and runs updates and removals.

    ModStore keeps one \l vsmm::ModEntry per installed mod, keyed by mod id.
    It is a QML singleton. It exposes the counts and the busy state as
    properties, and invokable methods to reload, update, mark, favorite and
    remove mods. Adding a mod goes through
    \l vsmm::ModLoader instead, which calls add().

    Before the first add(), call setConfig() and setGameMngr(). The store
    reads the favorite mods and the update settings from the config, and the
    game version and the mods folders from the game manager. It does not take
    ownership of either.

    When two zips in the mods folders have the same mod id, the store keeps
    the one with the higher version. A mod loaded as \l {vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType}{ModLoadType::GUI} is copied into
    the first mods folder. An update is copied next to the old zip. When
    \c deleteOldModVersion is set in the config, the old zip is moved to the
    trash.

    The \l workPending property is \c true while a reload or an update runs.
    It starts as \c true and turns \c false 500 ms after onModsReloaded() is
    called, unless a new reload starts first.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModStore::installedModsCount
    \brief The number of installed mods.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModStore::updatesCount
    \brief The number of installed mods with an update available.

    It shares its change signal with \l installedModsCount.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModStore::workPending
    \brief Whether a reload or an update runs.

    It starts as \c true and turns \c false 500 ms after the first scan and
    its online info requests finish. It stays \c true while the \c gameConfig
    path is empty or missing at startup, because no scan starts.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModStore::modsSelected
    \brief Whether at least one mod is marked for update.

    \sa markForUpdate()
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModStore::ModStore(QObject *parent)

    Constructs an empty store with the given \a parent.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::setConfig(vsmm::IConfig *config)

    Sets the user settings to \a config and loads the favorite mods from it.
    A second call only logs a warning. A null \a config is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::setGameMngr(vsmm::IGameMngr *gameMngr)

    Sets the game manager to \a gameMngr. The store reloads its mods whenever
    the mods folders of the game manager change. A second call only logs a
    warning. A null \a gameMngr is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::add(vsmm::ModLocalInfo localModInfo, vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType loadType)
    \reimp

    Ignores \a localModInfo when its id is empty, and handles it according to
    \a loadType otherwise.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::updateOnline(QStringView id, QJsonObject onlineInfo)
    \reimp

    Ignores \a onlineInfo when no mod with the id \a id is installed.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::reload()

    Drops all mods and starts a new scan of the mods folders. Sets
    \l workPending to \c true.

    The store emits modsReloading() before it drops the mods.
    \l vsmm::ModLoader starts the scan on that signal.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::update(const QString &id)

    Starts the update of the mod \a id. Does nothing when the mod is not
    installed, has no update, or \l workPending is \c true.

    \sa updateAll(), updateSelected()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::updateAll()

    Starts the update of every mod with an available update. Does nothing
    while \l workPending is \c true.

    \sa update(), updateSelected()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::updateSelected()

    Starts the update of the mods marked with markForUpdate() that have an
    update. Does nothing while \l workPending is \c true.

    \sa update(), updateAll()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::markForUpdate(const QString &id, bool marked)

    Marks or unmarks the mod \a id for updateSelected(), depending on
    \a marked. Does nothing when the mod is not installed.

    \sa modsSelected
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::setFavorite(const QString &id, bool favorite)

    Sets whether the mod \a id is a favorite, depending on \a favorite, and
    passes the new list of favorites to the config. Does nothing when the
    mod is not installed.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::remove(const QString &id)

    Deletes the zip of the mod \a id from disk and removes the mod from the
    store. The file is deleted, not moved to the trash. When the file cannot
    be deleted, the mod stays in the store.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModStore::contains(const QString &id) const

    Returns \c true when a mod with the id \a id is installed.
*/

/*!
    \fn const vsmm::ModEntry *vsmm::ModStore::find(const QString &id) const
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModStore::modsCount() const

    Returns the number of installed mods.

    \sa installedModsCount
*/

/*!
    \fn int vsmm::ModStore::modUpdatesCount() const

    Returns the number of installed mods with an update available.

    \sa updatesCount
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModStore::isWorkPending() const

    Returns \c true while a reload or an update runs.

    \sa workPending
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::modSelected()

    This signal is emitted when a mod is marked or unmarked for update. It is
    the change signal of \l modsSelected.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::modsChanged()

    This signal is emitted when the number of installed mods or of available
    updates can change. It is the change signal of \l installedModsCount and
    \l updatesCount.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::workChanged()

    This signal is emitted when \l workPending changes.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::onModsReloaded()
    \reimp

    Emits modsLoaded() and clears \l workPending after 500 ms.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::onModUpdateProgress(const QString &modId, qint64 received, qint64 total)
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModStore::onModUpdateFailed(QString modId, QString reason)
    \reimp
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModEntry
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief One installed mod, its local zip info and its online info.

    A ModEntry is built from the \l vsmm::ModLocalInfo of a mod zip. It keeps
    the id, name, version, authors and file of the zip. The description, side,
    dependencies and error of the local info are not kept.

    initOnlineInfo() adds the data from the mod API: the online name and
    author, tags, side, mod page URL, logo URL and the latest compatible
    release. Once online info is set, getName() and getAuthors() return the
    online values instead of the local ones.

    \l vsmm::ModStore owns the entries. Other classes get read access through
    \l vsmm::IModStore::find().
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief The newest release of a mod that can update the installed version.

    initOnlineInfo() fills it. Until then, and when no release qualifies,
    \l mHasUpdate is \c false, \l mUrl and \l mFileName are empty and
    \l mVersion holds the default \c 0.1.0.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion::mUrl

    Download URL of the release zip.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion::mVersion

    Version of the release.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion::mFileName

    File name of the release zip.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion::mSupportedVersions

    Game versions the release supports. \l vsmm::ModEntry does not fill it,
    so it is always empty.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion::mHasUpdate

    \c true when a release newer than the installed version was found.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModEntry::ModEntry(vsmm::ModLocalInfo info)

    Constructs an entry from the local zip info \a info. The entry has no
    online info and is neither marked for update nor a favorite.
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::ModEntry::toString() const

    Returns the mod as \c {id@version}, for example in log messages.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModEntry::operator QString() const

    Returns toString().
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringView vsmm::ModEntry::getId() const

    Returns the mod id.
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringView vsmm::ModEntry::getName() const

    Returns the online name, or the name from \c modinfo.json when the online
    name is empty.
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringList vsmm::ModEntry::getAuthors() const

    Returns the online author as a one item list, or the authors from
    \c modinfo.json when the online author is empty.
*/

/*!
    \fn const semver::version<> &vsmm::ModEntry::getVersion() const

    Returns the installed version.
*/

/*!
    \fn const QFileInfo &vsmm::ModEntry::getFileInfo() const

    Returns the file info of the installed zip.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModEntry::isMarkedForUpdate() const

    Returns \c true when the mod is marked for update.

    \sa setMarkedForUpdate()
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModEntry::isFavorite() const

    Returns \c true when the mod is a favorite.

    \sa setFavorite()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModEntry::setMarkedForUpdate(bool marked)

    Marks or unmarks the mod for update, depending on \a marked.

    \sa isMarkedForUpdate()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModEntry::setFavorite(bool favorite)

    Sets whether the mod is a favorite, depending on \a favorite.

    \sa isFavorite()
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModEntry::initOnlineInfo(QJsonObject json, const semver::version<> &gameVersion, bool cfgIncludePrerelease)

    Reads the online info from \a json, the \c mod object of the mod API
    response. A field with an unexpected type is logged and skipped.

    The latest version is the newest release that is newer than the installed
    version and has a tag with the same major and minor version as
    \a gameVersion. Prerelease versions count only when the installed version
    is a prerelease or \a cfgIncludePrerelease is \c true. When such a
    release exists, hasUpdate() returns \c true.

    \sa getLatestVersion()
*/

/*!
    \fn const QUrl &vsmm::ModEntry::getUrl() const

    Returns the mod page URL on the mod database. It uses the URL alias of
    the mod when it has one, and the asset id otherwise. The URL is empty
    until initOnlineInfo() is called.
*/

/*!
    \fn const vsmm::ModEntry::LatestVersion &vsmm::ModEntry::getLatestVersion() const

    Returns the latest release that can update the installed version.

    \sa hasUpdate(), initOnlineInfo()
*/

/*!
    \fn const QStringList &vsmm::ModEntry::getTags() const

    Returns the online tags of the mod.
*/

/*!
    \fn QStringView vsmm::ModEntry::getSide() const

    Returns the online side the mod runs on. It is empty until
    initOnlineInfo() is called.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModEntry::hasUpdate() const

    Returns \c true when a newer compatible release was found.

    \sa getLatestVersion()
*/

/*!
    \fn const QUrl &vsmm::ModEntry::getLogoUrl() const

    Returns the URL of the mod logo from the online info, or an empty URL
    when the online info has none.
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModLocalInfo
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Contents of a mod zip's \c modinfo.json.

    \l vsmm::ModLoader reads a ModLocalInfo from each mod zip and passes it
    to \l {vsmm::IModStore::add()}{IModStore::add()}. The struct is a
    Q_GADGET and QML gets it as the \c localModInfo value type from
    \l {vsmm::ModLoader::readLocalInfo()}{ModLoader::readLocalInfo()}.

    Fields missing from \c modinfo.json keep their defaults: \c None for the
    description, \c Unknown for the side and a list with \c Unknown for the
    authors. When the zip cannot be read, only \l mError is set.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::name
    \brief The display name, the same as \l mName.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::id
    \brief The mod id, the same as \l mId.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::description
    \brief The description, the same as \l mDescription.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::side
    \brief The side the mod runs on, the same as \l mSide.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::version
    \brief The mod version as a string.

    \sa versionString()
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::authors
    \brief The authors, the same as \l mAuthors.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::dependencies
    \brief The dependencies, the same as \l mDependencies.
*/

/*!
    \property vsmm::ModLocalInfo::error
    \brief Why the zip could not be read, the same as \l mError.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mName

    Display name.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mId

    Mod id.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mDescription

    Description, \c None by default.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mSide

    Side the mod runs on, \c Unknown by default.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mError

    Why the zip could not be read. Empty on success.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mAuthors

    Authors, a list with \c Unknown by default.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mDependencies

    Dependencies as \c {modId@version}, with \c * as the version when
    \c modinfo.json leaves it empty.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mVersion

    Mod version.
*/

/*!
    \variable vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mFileInfo

    File info of the mod zip.
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::ModLocalInfo::toString() const

    Returns the mod as \c {id@version}, for example in log messages.
*/

/*!
    \fn QString vsmm::ModLocalInfo::versionString() const

    Returns \l mVersion as a string.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModLocalInfo::operator QString() const

    Returns toString().
*/

/*!
    \class vsmm::ModLoader
    \inmodule VSMM
    \brief Reads mod zips, fetches online info and downloads updates.

    ModLoader scans the mods folders and reads \c modinfo.json from each zip
    on a worker thread. For each readable zip it calls
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::add()}{IModStore::add()}, then requests the online
    info of the mod from the mod API and passes it to
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::updateOnline()}{IModStore::updateOnline()}. When the
    mod id is disabled in the game, the loader disables the loaded version as
    well.

    The loader also downloads updates. It saves each download in the
    temporary folder and loads it as a
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType}{ModLoadType::Update}, so the store
    replaces the installed zip. When the
    downloaded zip has a different mod id, the update fails.

    It is a QML singleton. readLocalInfo() reads a zip without installing
    it, load() installs it. Both are invokable from QML.

    Call setGameMngr(), setHttpClient() and setStore() before the first scan.
    The loader does not take ownership of these objects. It counts loads and
    downloads in progress and emits allModsReloaded() when none are left.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModLoader::ModLoader()

    Constructs the loader. Zips are read and downloads are saved on two
    thread pools with at most four threads each.
*/

/*!
    \fn bool vsmm::ModLoader::initModsList()

    Scans the mods folders of the game manager and loads every readable
    \c .zip file in them. A folder that does not exist is skipped with a
    warning.

    Returns \c false when the game manager has no mods folders, and \c true
    otherwise.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::setHttpClient(vsmm::IHttpClient *httpClient)

    Sets the HTTP client for online info and downloads to \a httpClient. A
    second call only logs a warning. A null \a httpClient is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::setGameMngr(vsmm::IGameMngr *gameMngr)

    Sets the game manager to \a gameMngr. The loader reads the mods folders
    and the disabled mods from it. A second call only logs a warning. A null
    \a gameMngr is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::setStore(vsmm::IModStore *store)

    Sets the mod store to \a store and connects the loader to it. The loader
    starts a scan on \l {vsmm::IModStore::modsReloading()}{modsReloading()},
    downloads updates on
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::modUpdateRequested()}{modUpdateRequested()}, and
    allModsReloaded() calls
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::onModsReloaded()}{onModsReloaded()}. A second call
    only logs a warning. A null \a store is a fatal error.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::setApiUrl(QUrl apiUrl)

    Sets the base URL of the mod API to \a apiUrl. The mod id is appended to
    it for each request. The default is
    \c {https://mods.vintagestory.at/api/mod/}.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::load(QFileInfo &&fileInfo)

    Loads the zip \a fileInfo from a mods folder as a
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType}{ModLoadType::Init}. The zip is read on
    a worker thread.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::load(const QUrl &filePath)

    Loads the zip at the local file URL \a filePath as a
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::ModLoadType}{ModLoadType::GUI}, so the store copies
    it into the first mods folder, or installs it as an update when the mod
    id is already installed. The zip is read on a worker thread. A file that
    is not a readable mod zip is only logged.
*/

/*!
    \fn vsmm::ModLocalInfo vsmm::ModLoader::readLocalInfo(const QUrl &filePath)

    Reads \c modinfo.json from the zip at the local file URL \a filePath and
    returns it without installing anything. Runs on the calling thread.

    When the zip cannot be opened, has no \c modinfo.json, or its
    \c modinfo.json has no id or name or an invalid version, the result has
    only \l {vsmm::ModLocalInfo::mError}{mError} set.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::allModsReloaded()

    This signal is emitted when no loads or downloads are left in progress.
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::onModsReloading()

    Starts a new scan with initModsList().
*/

/*!
    \fn void vsmm::ModLoader::onModUpdateRequested(QStringList modIds)

    Downloads the latest version of each mod in \a modIds. The download
    progress goes to
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::onModUpdateProgress()}{IModStore::onModUpdateProgress()}
    and a failed download to
    \l {vsmm::IModStore::onModUpdateFailed()}{IModStore::onModUpdateFailed()}.
*/
